{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion` type implements\n`trust_but_verify::graph::Criterion<D>` for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    type Ok: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> NodeId<D>;\n    fn criterion_path(&self) -> CriterionPath;\n    fn version(&self) -> CriterionVersion;\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        ctx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement says every criterion type implements `Criterion<D>` for the application domain. It gives the trait shape: `Send + Sized`, an `Ok` type that is `Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send`, the methods `source_node_id`, `criterion_path` and `version`, and an `execute` that takes `self` and `&mut ValidationContext` and returns a `Send` future of `Result<Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>`.\n\nThe tests check this mostly at compile time, which is the only way to check a trait shape. Several test criteria implement the trait with exactly this signature: `Review` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs`, `Review` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs`, and `Review<O>` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs`. If the trait had a different shape, these impls would not compile.\n\nI map the obligations to tests as follows.\n- **`Ok` bounds and `Send` without `Sync`:** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` uses a `Cell<u32>` answer, which is `Send` but not `Sync`. It runs verify, store, load and refresh through a `send()` helper that requires the futures to be `Send`. This shows `Ok` needs only `Send`, not `Sync`. It also shows the `execute` future is `Send` and that `Ok` survives serialization and deserialization.\n- **The three identity methods are used and their values asserted:** `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts `source_node_id`, `criterion_path` and `version` on the verified and the reloaded record. `caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly` covers version compatibility. The `Review` impl's `source_node_id` bumps a `descriptor_reads` counter. `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` asserts the counter reads 1.\n- **`execute` behavior:** `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` runs a deterministic `execute` that uses `ValidationContext`. It asserts the output, the stored dependencies, and `NoAgentConfigured`. `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts the execution count and the stored JSON output, so it checks the `Ok` serialization.\n- **`Sized`:** the `Sized` supertrait and the trait's name and path can't be tested at runtime. Compilation of the impls and `public_exports_match_the_appendix` cover the export path.\n\nI found no gap.",
  "references": "a879f0ae49401bc00fac45ea5398c96091e5d5707b6490f80c3427a3894f1a04",
